build/
*.class
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

demo/*

# Everything npm and Next put on disk. None of it is anchored to viewer/,
# because a second one of these turns up the moment anybody runs npm anywhere
# else in the tree — viewer/.check already has its own .next.
#
# node_modules was 380 MB and 10,964 files, 96% of everything this repository
# tracked. It arrived whole with the viewer in 35ad1b0, at a point when this
# .gitignore knew only about build/, *.class and .DS_Store — a Java project's
# ignore file, which had no reason to expect a JavaScript directory. Nobody
# chose it. Its largest single file was 85 MB of Apple Silicon machine code:
# @next/swc-darwin-arm64, Next's Rust compiler, which npm installs to match
# the machine it is on and which is therefore useless to anyone on Linux.
#
# .next is the build cache, 109 MB that `next build` rewrites every time.
#
# package-lock.json is committed, so `npm ci` in viewer/ restores node_modules
# byte for byte. Nothing a student does needs either directory: viewer/out is
# the export they load, and it stays committed on purpose — like the generated
# protobuf sources — so that a student never runs npm at all.
node_modules/
.next/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Where s10-console.ts emits the views so it can render them without a browser.
viewer/.check/

# Gradle scratch state. The build outputs go to build/, which is already ignored.
.gradle/
